  "notes": ["ঔ has the diphthong ou, similar to “ow” in “cow.”","After a consonant, ঔ becomes ৌ (ঔ-কার): ক + ৌ = কৌ (kou). Words beginning with independent ঔ are relatively uncommon and often formal or Sanskrit-derived.","The everyday modern spelling of medicine is usually ওষুধ; ঔষধ is retained here as the traditional alphabet example."]
